    "explanation": "Outcome: the rider's claim is not made out and the fare stands. Both of you should read the two figures that decide it. This was a pooled trip (vehicle_type RYDE_POOL), and for pooled trips POL-RD-12 fixes the comparison at the matched-itinerary distance the platform computed at match time, read from trip_record.optimal_distance_km = 16.0 km ('matched pooled itinerary with one co-rider'). The 11.5 km in the rider's complaint is the separate solo_optimal_distance_km field, carried for reference only; a claim measured against it fails on that ground alone, and the rider's advocate rightly did not press it. Distance spent collecting a co-rider on a platform-matched pooled itinerary is never a deviation, and the driver's account of the co-rider pickup is corroborated by the trip record itself, not merely asserted.\n\nMeasured against the matched itinerary, the overrun is 0.96 km: 16.96 km on the GPS trace less 16.0 km. The trace figure governs over trip_record.actual_distance_km of 17.0 km, which POL-RD-01 treats as a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH more than 20% of the optimal distance AND more than 0.8 km absolute. The 0.96 km does clear the absolute limb, but 20% of 16.0 km is 3.2 km, and 0.96 km is 6.00%. The relative limb fails, both limbs must pass, and no route deviation is established. POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION in that event, save for a billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4), to which I turn below.\n\nBecause no deviation is established, POL-RD-02 does not run and no fare recomputation issues. For transparency only: on these figures it would have produced a recomputed fare of $22.76 against the $23.51 charged, a $0.75 refund before rounding, but the clause applies only where POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation. POL-RD-09 gives nothing either. The fare breakdown carries no ERP or toll lines (0.00, erp_gantries empty), no airport surcharge (0.00) on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, and no promo or waiting-time anomaly. The distance line billed at 17.0 km matches the trace's 16.96 km within round convention, so it is not a phantom line and there is no unmatched charge line in the ledger. No POL-RD-09(4) finding arises and no referral follows.\n\nThe GPS trace is clean at policy level: 133 fixes, 100.0% coverage, a 10-second sampling interval, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) do not fire and no impaired-trace handling or POL-RD-10(3) escalation applies. No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-02860-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 could not have been run had a closure been asserted; no traffic cause was in fact asserted by either party, and the driver's answer rests on the pooled baseline in the trip record. The chat log carries zero messages and both amendment timestamps are null, so POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 have nothing to operate on. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires, and no clause produces a referral.\n\nThe rider's remaining points are answered. That the measured 0.96 km clears the 0.8 km absolute limb is accepted, but POL-RD-01 requires both limbs and the relative limb fails. That the rider was billed 17.0 km rather than the 16.0 km itinerary is not a billing defect: the meter charges the distance actually driven (16.96 km, rounded to 17.0 km), and the matched itinerary is the comparator for the deviation test, not a cap on the bill. The driver's profile decided nothing either way: no material deviation arises (6.00% is far below 50% and 0.96 km far below 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 check is not engaged and no conduct referral or uplift follows; and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d of 0 adds no corroboration burden under POL-RD-08.\n\nEverything this ruling rests on carries weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-02860 and EV-GPS-02860), so confidence is not discounted, and the missing advisory at weight 0.0 carries no fact. The monetary effect is nil, below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; either party may appeal it once under POL-GEN-04 within 30 days."
