    "explanation": "To the rider: your dispute is not upheld and the SGD 23.51 charge stands. This was a RYDE_POOL trip (trip_record.vehicle_type, EV-TRIP-02860), so under POL-RD-12 the comparator is the matched-itinerary optimal of 16.0 km that the routing engine computed for the pooled itinerary with one co-rider (trip_record.optimal_distance_km and optimal_route_source, EV-TRIP-02860). The 11.5 km you call your usual route is trip_record.solo_optimal_distance_km, carried for reference only; POL-RD-12 says a claim measured against it has cited the wrong field and fails on that ground alone, and both advocates accept that. The governing distance is the trace: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 16.96 km (EV-GPS-02860), and the 17.0 km on the trip record is a rounded convenience copy that POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test. Excess is therefore 0.96 km, or 6.00% of the 16.0 km baseline. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH more than 20% of optimal AND more than 0.8 km; the 0.96 km clears the absolute limb but 6.00% fails the relative limb, and both must pass. No deviation is established, so the POL-RD-02 recomputation does not run and the co-rider kilometres you are complaining about are inside the matched-itinerary baseline, which POL-RD-12 excludes from excess before POL-RD-01 is applied. For transparency only, on the figures your own advocate put up the recomputation would have been charged_total 23.51 less a recomputed fare of 22.76, a refund of 0.75 above the 0.50 de minimis - but the threshold test is a precondition and it is not met, so no refund issues. To the driver: the pooled baseline is applied in your favour and no exculpatory clause was needed. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes - 133 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0 (EV-GPS-02860) - so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) does not fire. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered (6.00% is below the 50% limb and 0.96 km below the 8.0 km limb, so there is no MATERIAL deviation) and would fail on the fields the clause names in any event: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 185 completed trips in 90 days, a ratio of 0.00, well under 0.05. No conduct referral follows. Neither party asserts an external traffic cause, so POL-RD-03 and POL-RD-13 have nothing to weigh; the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02860-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, both sides disclosed that, and its absence decides nothing here. There is no billing-integrity defect: the fare ledger (EV-FARE-02860) carries no ERP or toll lines, no airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, and bills 17.0 km against a 16.96 km trace, a rounding difference rather than a phantom line, so POL-RD-09(4) is not engaged and produces no referral. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: confidence is not below 0.70, the trip identifiers match across the trip record, trace and ledger, the trace is unimpaired, the timestamps agree, no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact, the refund is nil rather than above SGD 150.00, the two sides do not contradict each other, and every charge line has a counterpart in the trace or the trip record. Confidence is 0.90: the deciding facts - the 16.0 km matched-itinerary baseline and the 16.96 km trace distance, giving the 0.96 km / 6.00% excess - are carried by EV-TRIP-02860 and EV-GPS-02860, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so under POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is 1.0 and the bundle mean is context only. The monetary effect is zero, below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, and this provisional ruling carries the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
